WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.547
(uptempo music)

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.040
- [Narrator] While canyoneering
is a brand-new sport,

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.320
it starts with an
old-school leap of faith.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.640
Its participants hold their
breath as they rappel down

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.969
seemingly bottomless canyons formed

00:00:20.969 --> 00:00:23.600
by centuries of wind and water.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.491
Through oncoming waterfalls,
around blind turns

00:00:26.491 --> 00:00:28.989
and dangling over cliffs,
the sport’s pioneers

00:00:28.989 --> 00:00:32.221
take on natural wonders the
rest of us would never dare.

00:00:32.221 --> 00:00:34.869
Kitt Turner is one of those pioneers.

00:00:34.869 --> 00:00:36.533
He and and his team are
about to enter Canada's

00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:38.561
Box Canyon for the first time,

00:00:38.561 --> 00:00:41.978
a place that will make their knees quake.

00:00:47.883 --> 00:00:50.123
(uptempo music)

00:00:50.123 --> 00:00:53.472
- I got started running canyons in Hawaii.

00:00:53.472 --> 00:00:56.141
I started rock climbing
and eventually made

00:00:56.141 --> 00:00:59.571
the progression into canyoneering.

00:00:59.571 --> 00:01:01.072
Jenna's my girlfriend.

00:01:01.072 --> 00:01:04.112
She's a Hawaii girl, born and raised.

00:01:04.112 --> 00:01:07.021
We've been dating now
for almost two years.

00:01:07.021 --> 00:01:08.461
We met climbing.

00:01:08.461 --> 00:01:10.403
- Kitt always pushes me to go outside

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.403
my comfort level, a lot.

00:01:15.595 --> 00:01:18.404
(dramatic music)

00:01:18.404 --> 00:01:20.829
- [Kitt] When you're
talking about canyoneering,

00:01:20.829 --> 00:01:23.222
the process of descending a canyon,

00:01:23.222 --> 00:01:25.894
you have to decide how much
rope you wanna bring along.

00:01:25.894 --> 00:01:29.280
You wanna decide if the rock
quality is gonna be good

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.909
enough to set up anchors for the rappels.

00:01:32.909 --> 00:01:35.652
You also have to find a good crew

00:01:35.652 --> 00:01:37.812
that is good under pressure.

00:01:37.812 --> 00:01:40.153
- You're just dealing with
lots of complexities of nature.

00:01:40.153 --> 00:01:41.570
Rocks, waterfall,

00:01:42.421 --> 00:01:45.393
it's just constant problem
solving, using your brain,

00:01:45.393 --> 00:01:46.412
using your body.

00:01:46.412 --> 00:01:48.381
- Canyons are very fickle,

00:01:48.381 --> 00:01:50.781
and they're very weather dependent.

00:01:50.781 --> 00:01:52.713
Conditions in a canyon can change

00:01:52.713 --> 00:01:56.313
from one day to the next,
from one season to the next.

00:01:56.313 --> 00:01:59.542
(upbeat music)

00:01:59.542 --> 00:02:02.593
For this particular canyon, Box Canyon,

00:02:02.593 --> 00:02:04.962
you have to cross the Squamish River.

00:02:04.962 --> 00:02:07.694
- [Jenna] Kayaking across
the river was an ordeal

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:10.553
because you just really have
to paddle your heart out

00:02:10.553 --> 00:02:13.433
just to cut across that current.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.953
And then you have to make a sharp U-turn

00:02:15.953 --> 00:02:18.444
into this little tiny beachfront.

00:02:18.444 --> 00:02:20.193
- [Kitt] So once you cross the river,

00:02:20.193 --> 00:02:22.254
there's a mosquito-infested hike

00:02:22.254 --> 00:02:25.774
into kind of the bottom
of the Box Canyon stream.

00:02:25.774 --> 00:02:28.382
And then you hike upstream for a while

00:02:28.382 --> 00:02:31.602
before you get to the
technical part of the canyon,

00:02:31.602 --> 00:02:33.353
which involves rope.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:35.172
- The first thought was, is this man-made?

00:02:35.172 --> 00:02:36.884
This is not real.

00:02:36.884 --> 00:02:38.444
It looks like a

00:02:38.444 --> 00:02:40.353
Disneyland ride.

00:02:40.353 --> 00:02:41.853
- One, two, three.

00:02:48.831 --> 00:02:52.331
Box Canyon is considered a Class C canyon.

00:02:57.345 --> 00:03:00.094
Most of the rappels if not all the rappels

00:03:00.094 --> 00:03:02.802
you're going straight
through the water course,

00:03:02.802 --> 00:03:04.604
which is straight through the waterfall

00:03:04.604 --> 00:03:07.591
and you're getting pounded by the water.

00:03:07.591 --> 00:03:09.473
It's hitting you in your face.

00:03:09.473 --> 00:03:12.142
You're slipping, you're
sliding all over the place.

00:03:12.142 --> 00:03:14.142
- [Jenna] My favorite thing
about dropping into a canyon

00:03:14.142 --> 00:03:16.753
is the rush of getting over the edge.

00:03:16.753 --> 00:03:17.902
- This is my passion, man.

00:03:17.902 --> 00:03:19.772
I don't get more pumped
than when I'm in a canyon.

00:03:19.772 --> 00:03:22.553
- [Kitt] It kinda adds
that element of excitement

00:03:22.553 --> 00:03:25.351
where you can't see where
you're gonna end up.

00:03:25.351 --> 00:03:27.271
(yelling)

00:03:27.271 --> 00:03:30.390
- [Jenna] When you're on
the edge as an adventurer,

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.350
when you feel like I could
die doing this right now

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:36.612
but I can't back down, and then you do it,

00:03:36.612 --> 00:03:38.521
it's like the most amazing feeling.

00:03:38.521 --> 00:03:39.354
Woo, yeah.

00:03:40.561 --> 00:03:43.970
I don't get the people that are
like, why would you do that?

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:46.390
I'm just like, why not?

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:48.721
If you don't get it, you don't get it.

00:03:48.721 --> 00:03:50.502
- For someone who's looking

00:03:50.502 --> 00:03:53.170
at doing what we did, which
is dropping everything

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:55.342
and pursuing your dreams,

00:03:55.342 --> 00:03:59.281
I would say that it's
definitely a leap of faith.

00:03:59.281 --> 00:04:01.230
And maybe you crash and burn,

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:04.050
but the highs are incredible
and you're never gonna get

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:07.812
those amazing moments and see if you

00:04:07.812 --> 00:04:12.022
can really achieve your
dreams if you don't try.

00:04:12.022 --> 00:04:14.439
(soft music)

